  "adaptations": [
    "All twelve original module bodies retain their matcher patterns, callback/function bindings and arities, original AST allocation and mutation statements, branch order and warning text. Every original string, numeric and regular-expression literal is retained; only Webpack module identifier strings become statically named lazy imports.",
    "The two local runtime.ts files supply finite checked views of AST values captured by the original f-matches patterns. They return the original AST objects and source arrays without copies. Unknown capture values are narrowed only after their original successful-match checks or at original field/method reads.",
    "Function and class expressions still receive the original in-place type and id assignments; an arrow expression body is still wrapped by the original BlockStatement/ReturnStatement allocations. Checked declaration views observe the updated nodes after those writes.",
    "Includes retains its original descriptor-aware object-spread helper, symbol-key filtering, key order, _defineProperty behavior, comparisons and all Object descriptor operations. Overload signatures type its variable argument list without changing the implementation parameter count or arguments reads.",
    "The existing self-reassigning _typeof helper uses a var function initializer because strict TypeScript rejects assignment to a function declaration. Its inferred function name, parameter binding, arity, self-assignment and bodies are retained; the source audit accounts for that binding-preserving form.",
    "Original optional parent and replacement-result phases use erased non-null annotations; no new runtime sentinel rejection is added. The original comma expressions retain the same operands while redundant non-null parentheses are removed to satisfy strict TypeScript."
  ]
